# Live installer environment.
#
# Kept small on purpose. Every package here is code running on an unconfigured
# machine on an unknown network, before any of this project's protections
# exist, and it is also the thing that has to boot on hardware we have never
# seen.

base
linux
linux-firmware
intel-ucode
amd-ucode
archiso
mkinitcpio-archiso

# Boot loaders. syslinux is required by the 'bios.syslinux' boot mode; the UEFI
# path uses systemd-boot from systemd, which base already provides.
syslinux
memtest86+
memtest86+-efi

# Installer. steel-installer carries the sequence and the SteelOS modules; see
# packages/steel-installer.
calamares
steel-installer
qt6-base
qt6-declarative
qt6-svg
kpmcore
squashfs-tools
rsync

# Fonts. The installer draws its own pages, and a live medium with no font
# renders every one of them as boxes — which looks like a broken ISO rather
# than a missing package.
noto-fonts
ttf-dejavu

# A desktop, because a graphical installer needs one. Wayland, matching what
# gets installed. plasma-workspace provides the Wayland session directly —
# there is no longer a separate plasma-wayland-session package.
plasma-desktop
plasma-workspace
sddm
konsole
dolphin
firefox

# Everything the installer's modules call into.
sbctl
tpm2-tools
cryptsetup
btrfs-progs
erofs-utils
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
gptfdisk
mtools
systemd-ukify

# SteelOS tooling, so the installed system's own tools do the work rather than
# a parallel implementation that can drift.
steel-check
steel-config
steel-boot
steel-duress

# Hardware diagnosis, for the machines where installation will not be simple.
pciutils
usbutils
dmidecode
efibootmgr
inxi

# Recovery, because a live ISO is also the tool people reach for when an
# installed machine will not boot.
restic
borg
age
vim
less
man-db
networkmanager
